3. **Title: Multi-Scale Correlation of Density and Vorticity**
   Research Objective: Investigate the spatial coupling between density fluctuations and local vorticity magnitude across different scales. The goal is to determine if mass density "clumping" acts as a dynamical barrier to the intensification of small-scale vortex structures.

4. **Title: Helicity Flux and Mirror Symmetry Breaking**
   Research Objective: Calculate the local and global helicity density over the 1001-snapshot time series. This research aims to assess whether the solenoidal forcing induces spontaneous parity-breaking in the velocity field, leading to sustained localized helical structures.

5. **Title: Spectral Energy Bottlenecks at the Forcing Scale**
   Research Objective: Examine the energy spectrum near the injection scale (n=2) to identify potential "bottleneck" effects where energy accumulates before cascading to smaller scales. This will evaluate how the specific correlation time of the driving force influences the spectral slope in the inertial range.

6. **Title: Lagrangian Coherent Structures (LCS) and Transport Barriers**
   Research Objective: Identify Lagrangian Coherent Structures by analyzing the Finite-Time Lyapunov Exponent (FTLE) fields derived from the velocity data. The research objective is to map these "hidden" manifolds to determine if they act as absolute boundaries for fluid transport in the periodic box.

7. **Title: Statistical Mechanics of Vortex Merging Events**
   Research Objective: Model vortex interaction as a discrete event-based system to characterize the frequency and spatial distribution of vortex mergers and splits. This analysis will determine if these topological transitions follow a Poisson process or exhibit temporal clustering governed by local flow conditions.

8. **Title: Velocity Gradient Tensor Invariants in Turbulent Dissipation**
   Research Objective: Map the distribution of the velocity gradient tensor invariants (Q and R) throughout the 128³ domain over time. The objective is to identify the "teardrop" shape evolution in the Q-R plane and determine how frequently local flow regions transition between vortex-dominated and strain-dominated regimes.

9. **Title: Spatio-Temporal Intermittency of Dissipation Rates**
   Research Objective: Evaluate the spatial intermittency of the energy dissipation rate by calculating the probability density functions of local strain rates at varying spatial offsets. This seeks to clarify if the dissipation is concentrated in specific "sheets" or "filaments" and how this intermittency evolves as the simulation reaches a statistically steady state.

10. **Title: Acoustic Signature of Subsonic Turbulence**
   Research Objective: By decomposing the velocity field into solenoidal and compressive components, determine the fraction of kinetic energy that manifests as pressure-driven acoustic waves. This research aims to quantify the "noise" generated by the turbulence within the isothermal unit box.
